        },
        "heading_1": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "You're Not Imagining This — And You're Not Alone",
            "heading_size": "h0",
            "heading_alignment": "center",
            "heading_mobilealignment": "center",
            "heading_color": "#14312d"
          }
        },
        "text_1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Maybe it started small — a raspy feeling by the afternoon, a blink that didn't quite do its job, eyes that felt raw by the time you got into bed. Somewhere around your 40s, something changed, and it's easy to start wondering if it's really happening or if you're just tired, stressed, staring at screens too much.</p><p>You're not imagining it, and you're not overreacting. Perimenopausal dry eye is real, it's hormone-driven, and it's far more common than most people realize — most of them just aren't talking about it. We are. Here's what's actually happening, backed by real numbers, and what genuinely helps.</p>",
            "text_style": "subtitle",
            "text_alignment": "center",
            "text_mobilealignment": "center",
            "text_color": "#3f5854"
          }
        },
        "button_1": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "See What Can Help",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_link_newtab": false,
